From 71aeee4ee573f8f85be8c87504305ba3810b02f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ga=C3=ABl=20Duval?= <gael@murena.io>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 12:52:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] fix(word): built-in heading styles use the theme heading
 font

Heading 1-9, their linked character styles and Title were created with a
fixed Arial font. Word's built-in (latent) definitions use the theme
heading font (+Headings: majorHAnsi/majorEastAsia/majorBidi), so a style
applied to a document that does not define it follows the document
theme: Calibri Light in a Calibri document, Cambria in a Cambria one.

[upstreamable]

Assisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
